comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T16:56:18.081Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence that the transition half of this policy engine has no substrate at all today, measured on a sandbox tracker at build 2026.7.29.\n\nWhat is declared. The workspace schema file schema/workflows.json contains exactly six entries, and all six are role-to-status-name aliases: draft_status, open_status, in_progress_status, blocked_status, close_status, canceled_status. There is no transition list, no guard, no precondition and no required-field rule anywhere in schema data. So the lifecycle state machine exists only as control flow inside the mutation paths, and nothing publishes it.\n\nWhat that permits. A closed item moved to in_progress through update --status succeeds, exit 0, changed_field_count 4. A closed item moved to draft succeeds - into a tier the corpus has never once written, 0 of 40,856 entries. Closing an already-closed item succeeds and overwrites the stored close reason. None of the three emits a warning.\n\nWhy this matters beyond tidiness. Custom statuses can be registered with a lifecycle role, so a domain pack can add states; it cannot say which states may follow which, who may perform the move, or what must be supplied. That makes the universal-customization claim thin in exactly the place a non-software domain needs it most: a review state that anyone can leave, an approval that requires no approver. It also means an agent - or a reinforcement-learning policy treating the mutation surface as an action space - has no machine-readable way to enumerate the legal actions for an item in a given state, so legality can only be discovered by attempting a mutation and reading the outcome.\n\nScope note. The specific reopen transition and the clearing of terminal fields belong to pm-83cz0o. What is recorded here is the absence of a declared transition relation for this engine to enforce.\n"
  "2026-09-08T15:00:44.688Z","harness:codex","Live lineage correction: pm-f4r1 shipped per-type allowed transitions and pm-hx23u5 shipped transactional extension mutation guards. Current implementation confirms both foundations exist. This delivery extends them with data-declared subjects, transition/field/approval/authorship rules, advisory defaults and opt-in refusal; identity remains unverified workflow provenance. Full all-status CLI inventory inspected: 2721 items, completeness complete, no truncation. Related completeness work reuses pm-htbetn; no duplicate created."
  "2026-09-08T15:31:41.797Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: pure declaration parsing, bounded policy IO, transactional lifecycle/import enforcement, content-bound independent approvals, public SDK authoring and CLI/MCP schema verbs are implemented. Thirteen focused SDK/CLI tests and a real MCP handler parity scenario pass; typecheck and focused ESLint pass. Repository-wide coverage and compatibility gates are now running. Approval identities are explicitly documented as unverified workflow provenance."
  "2026-09-08T15:41:46.875Z","harness:codex","Review hardening note: refusal diagnostics must identify the rule as well as the policy and remain bounded when many declarations refuse. The full shared policy decision set stays in the audit event; user-facing summaries will cap displayed policies and field paths. Additional real filesystem tests will cover import, delete and restore so no alternate write route relies solely on adapter inference."
  "2026-09-08T16:01:28.753Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: focused policy source coverage is exact 100/100/100/100 (311 statements, 294 branches, 70 functions, 249 lines), with 18 real parser/filesystem/CLI scenarios and no mocks or coverage ignores added. Draft 2020-12 JSON Schema validates independently with all builtin presets and unsafe-path negative controls. Pure evaluation benchmark: 10000 empty-policy evaluations 5.94ms; 10000 eight-policy evaluations 696.56ms; 1000 maximum-256-policy evaluations 1825.84ms. These measure evaluator cost, not end-to-end filesystem latency. Canonical flag budgets reflect exactly three new schema inputs; help token ceilings are preserved."
  "2026-09-08T16:04:52.788Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance passed in a newly initialized temporary tracker using the built CLI: authored approval and required-field policies; enabled refusal; verified a failed close preserves item history byte-for-byte; recorded an independent content-bound approval; closed with resolution/expected/actual evidence; strict completeness and direct history verification both passed. Live graph audit covers 2722 records and 13578 edges with no missing nodes, no isolates, no degree-one nodes, and acyclic ordering; informational findings concern seven historical hierarchy records, not new ordering failures. pm-changelog installed and registry latest both resolve to 2026.9.8."
  "2026-09-08T16:08:04.775Z","harness:codex","SDK migration evidence: documented schema contract 4.16, additive WorkflowPolicyActionResult discriminant, checkCompleteness option, and completeness result check for exhaustive consumers."
  "2026-09-08T16:21:13.237Z","harness:codex","Coverage diagnosis: the complete 651-file/8614-test run now has no assertion failures, but the helper named runCliInProcess executes the built CLI and cannot instrument the source registration branch. The transport parity test now invokes the real Commander registration directly and verifies persisted policy mode through PmClient; no mocked dispatch or exclusion is used."
  "2026-09-08T16:30:28.196Z","harness:codex","Static gate found a help-contract regression: shortening the schema operand description removed the Required; marker used by structured help to expose semantic requiredness. Restored that marker while retaining the compact text; the CLI still permits custom-type shorthand and rejects an absent operand through its existing actionable error."
  "2026-09-08T16:37:46.724Z","harness:codex","Final local test evidence: all 8615 tests in 652 files pass; coverage is exact 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered statements, branches, functions or lines. Compatible @types/node 26.5.0 is now installed after the existing release-age window; runtime dependency range >=22 is preserved. Build, all four TypeScript projects, contract snapshot and generated capability freshness pass after the update."
  "2026-09-08T16:50:56.781Z","harness:codex","Final implementation evidence: All 8615 tests pass at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. Real SDK, CLI, MCP, import, delete and restore scenarios pass; isolated manual acceptance verifies atomic refusal, independent approval and evidence-backed closure. Build, typecheck, contracts and linked tests pass."
  "2026-09-08T16:55:45.225Z","harness:codex","Pre-merge TDD evidence: a policy effect supplied as an array containing refuse was accepted because String coercion matched the vocabulary, then its non-string value bypassed effective refusal. The regression failed before the fix. Parsing now requires the actual value to be a string before checking the accepted set, and the existing malformed-vocabulary table covers array and null inputs."
  "2026-09-08T16:59:10.609Z","harness:codex","The hardened parser passes all 19 focused policy/completeness/MCP scenarios and retains exact policy source coverage: 311 statements, 295 branches, 70 functions, 249 lines, all covered. A separate temporary-tracker compiled CLI check rejects the malformed array effect with workflow_policy_invalid and leaves the registry absent. No mocks or exclusions were added."
  "2026-09-08T17:21:04.771Z","harness:codex","Review corrections: reject non-string policy effects; approval applies only to existing item transitions and validates current content on deletion, allowing creation without an impossible preexisting approval; expose definition/policy/message/dryRun in both MCP argument locations; retain the common schema profiling epilogue. Extract bounded edge and approval matching to satisfy static complexity limits without exemptions. Regression checks include real SDK, compiled CLI and MCP operations."
  "2026-09-08T17:24:48.473Z","harness:codex","Review round 1 validation: 26 focused tests pass across policy evaluation/storage, completeness, real MCP/CLI parity, enum recovery and list help. Direct static-quality gate passes with zero violations and exact 100 percent source/export/member docstring coverage, without threshold changes. Greptile CLI reports free review quota exhausted; Sourcery reports weekly 250000-diff-character quota exhausted. These are review availability limitations, not approvals. CodeRabbit findings have individual reactions and replies; full coverage is running before the next push."
  "2026-09-08T17:27:21.555Z","harness:codex","Manual review-fix acceptance passed in a fresh temporary tracker using separate compiled CLI processes: create under global approval refusal mode; refuse deletion without approval (exit 4); record independent approval; refuse same-actor deletion; preview deletion without removing the item; delete as the writer; verify all three immutable history entries with zero errors. Both PM roots were sandboxed and telemetry disabled for the fixture."
  "2026-09-08T17:30:00.788Z","harness:codex","Hosted review availability detail: cubic completed its check as neutral because its monthly review line limit is exhausted (40392 of 40000; provider states October 1 reset). No source finding or approval was returned by that check. CodeRabbit supplied the actionable first-round review; Greptile and Sourcery quota limitations remain separately recorded."
  "2026-09-08T17:32:19.918Z","harness:codex","Final review-correction evidence for PR #1224: All 8619 tests in 652 files pass with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. All linked policy tests, manual compiled CLI reviewed-deletion acceptance, build, typecheck, contracts and static quality pass. Docstring coverage is 100 percent; no new exclusions or relaxed limits."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T16:21:40.696Z","harness:codex","Mutation policy checks should run under the item lock before persistence; retain complete decisions in immutable history while bounding user-facing diagnostics. Approval fingerprints must bind the complete policy revision and reviewed content, and actor provenance must not be presented as authentication."
